  base images, one per image release, shared by the VMs made from it:
      <libvirt pool>/vmclaude-base-IMAGE-CHECKSUM.qcow2
  each VM's own disk (only what differs from its base image):
      <libvirt pool>/NAME.qcow2
  each VM's cloud-init settings (user, SSH key):
      <libvirt pool>/NAME-seed.iso

The pool is "$CREATE_POOL" (usually /var/lib/libvirt/images); set VMCLAUDE_POOL
for another. Free the space of unused images with "vmclaude prune".
EOF
      ;;
    prune) cat <<EOF
vmclaude prune [--uri URI]

Deletes base images in the libvirt pool that no VM disk is built on, and the
