Options:
  --keep        leave the VM running this time
  --no-tmux     run Claude directly, without tmux
  --hold        keep the terminal open after an error (used by app-menu launchers)
  -- ARGS       everything after -- goes to Claude

Examples:
  vmclaude dev
  vmclaude dev --continue                    continue the last conversation
  vmclaude connect dev -- --model opus       pass options to Claude
  vmclaude                                   the default VM
EOF
      ;;
    shell) cat <<EOF
vmclaude shell [--keep] NAME [COMMAND...]

Opens a normal shell on the VM (without starting Claude), or runs one command
there and prints its output. A libvirt VM is started if it is off. When you
leave the shell, the VM shuts down like after connect (see "vmclaude help
autostop"); --keep leaves it on. A single COMMAND never shuts it down.

Examples:
  vmclaude shell dev
  vmclaude shell dev df -h
  vmclaude shell dev 'cd ~/work && git status'
EOF
