vmclaude autostop NAME on|off

With "on" (the default for libvirt VMs), the VM shuts down when you leave
Claude ("vmclaude NAME") or "vmclaude shell NAME", so it does not use RAM and
CPU in the background. It stays on, and says why, while something still uses
it:
  - Claude left running in tmux (you pressed Ctrl-b d)
  - another vmclaude connect, shell or mount to this VM from this computer
  - someone logged in on the VM (another SSH login; on Windows, the screen)
  - a Claude process still running on the VM
It also stays on when the connection broke rather than ended.
"vmclaude NAME --keep" leaves it on once. Plain ssh logins (autostart) do not
shut it down: vmclaude is not running then.

Examples:
  vmclaude autostop dev off          the VM keeps running after you leave
  vmclaude autostop dev on
  vmclaude stop dev                  shut it down by hand
EOF
