vmclaude login NAME [--remove]

Logs Claude Code on the VM in, so it never shows its login screen there
(whose long link is hard to copy out of a terminal). The login happens on
THIS computer, with its browser:
  1. "claude setup-token" runs here and opens your browser; confirm there.
  2. vmclaude takes the long-lived token it prints (no copy and paste) and
     stores it on the VM in ~/.config/vmclaude/claude-env, readable only by
     your user there.
  3. Claude on the VM uses it from then on, however you start it.
Needs Claude Code on this computer and a Claude subscription. If the token
cannot be read automatically, you are asked to paste it (hidden input).
An API key (sk-ant-api...) works too: echo "\$ANTHROPIC_API_KEY" | vmclaude login NAME

Tokens made this way can only be used for chatting and coding (no remote-
control features); for those, use /login inside Claude instead.

Options:
  --remove      delete the stored token from the VM

Examples:
  vmclaude login arch
  vmclaude login win10
  claude setup-token            (by hand) then: vmclaude login arch   and paste it
  vmclaude login arch --remove
EOF
