vmclaude mount NAME [FOLDER]
vmclaude umount NAME [FOLDER]

Makes the VM's working folder (the profile's DIR, or the home folder) appear
as a folder on this computer, over SSH (sshfs). Programs here, Claude Code
included, then read and edit the VM's files as if they were local.
FOLDER defaults to ~/vm/NAME and must be empty. Needs sshfs
(Debian/Ubuntu: sudo apt install sshfs). The VM is started if it is off.

Mind: commands started in that folder still run on THIS computer, with its
programs. To run them in the VM use "vmclaude shell NAME 'COMMAND'", or the
run tool of "vmclaude mcp NAME --add".

Examples:
  vmclaude mount arch               ~/vm/arch is now the VM's home folder
  cd ~/vm/arch && claude            edit the VM's files with Claude Code here
  vmclaude shell arch 'make test'   run things in the VM
  vmclaude umount arch
EOF
      ;;
    mcp) cat <<EOF
vmclaude mcp NAME [--add]

Lets Claude Code running on this computer work inside the VM: it gets four
tools that act in the VM over SSH:
  run          run a command (bash on Linux, PowerShell on Windows VMs)
  read_file    read a file, with line numbers
  write_file   create or overwrite a file (folders are created)
  edit_file    replace exact text in a file, like Claude's own Edit
Paths are relative to the profile's DIR (or the home folder); ~ works.
The VM is started if it is off. Files move over SFTP, so size and special
characters do not matter.

  vmclaude mcp NAME --add   register it once, for all your projects:
                            claude mcp add --scope user NAME -- vmclaude mcp NAME
  vmclaude mcp NAME         the server itself; Claude Code starts it

Examples:
  vmclaude mcp arch --add
  claude                        then ask: "arch VM'inde ~/work/app.py yaz ve çalıştır"
  claude mcp remove arch --scope user        unregister

Needs python3 on this computer. In Claude Code, /mcp shows the server.
EOF
      ;;
